  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 1258 AM CDT Wed Aug 13 2026\n\nThe upper-level ridge of high pressure will remain in place \nacross the region Friday into the weekend. Highs will warm into \nthe middle 90s to around 100 each day with heat index values \naround 105 to 110. Warm overnight lows will also continue each \nnight with lows in the middle 70s to the lower 80s. The Extreme \nHeat Warning will remain in effect for the entire area through \nSunday. \n\nA complex of storms is expected to develop across the Plains \nagain Thursday night and push southeast. A drier air mass will \nadvect into the area, but is it possible that a few showers and \nstorms push into the far northern portions of the area Friday \nafternoon, north of Highway 54, as the complex weakens as it \nmoves southeast towards the area. Most locations will likely \nremain dry. Mainly dry conditions are expected this weekend. \n\nEarly next week, an upper-level disturbance will push the ridge\nback to the west and bring slightly cooler conditions to the \narea, especially the eastern portions of the area, as well as \nsome scattered shower and thunderstorm chances. The hotter \nconditions could linger across extreme southeastern Kansas and \nfar western Missouri next week.",
